# Several files here are checked byte-for-byte against a fresh build -- the exported
# tables by `tools/export_tables.py --check`, the two pages by `tools/build_app.py
# --check` -- and the pages are the source files inlined verbatim. Left to
# core.autocrlf, git rewrites their line endings on checkout and those checks then fail
# on whichever machine did not write them: the tables are written with an explicit CRLF
# terminator, everything else with LF. So git converts none of them.
data/*.csv          -text
data/geojson/*.geojson -text
data/gerbil_atlas.json -text
data/skull.json     -text
data/vec.json       -text
*.html              -text
corrections/*.json  -text
src/app.js          -text
src/app.css         -text
src/fixer.js        -text
src/fixer.css       -text

# CHANGELOG.md is added to at the same place by every change, so two branches conflict
# there for no reason. `union` keeps both sides. A local merge honors it -- which is where
# tools/corrections.py rebase merges -- and the web merge of a branch already current
# with main has nothing to resolve.
CHANGELOG.md        merge=union
# Derived and large: the numbers a change moves are in `corrections.py report`, and a
# textual diff of a 20 MB line or a gzip shows nothing.
data/gerbil_atlas_volumes.json -diff
data/gerbil_atlas_labels.nii.gz -diff
